  "caption": "Quinn clashed heads at Saturday footy, felt foggy, and soon begged to go back on. The answer was no.\n\nWith a suspected concussion, the player comes off, doesn't return that day, and gets a medical assessment. Most concussions don't involve being knocked out, and feeling fine soon after doesn't mean it's safe to play.\n\nWhat often helps: a day or two of relative rest, then light activity below the level that stirs up symptoms, stepping through a graded return (daily activity, light cardio, sport drills, non-contact training) and only returning to contact after medical clearance. Weeks in a dark room is outdated.\n\nCall an ambulance for worsening drowsiness, repeated vomiting, a seizure, a worsening headache, neck pain after impact or increasing confusion.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
